<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mehrab Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1839">1839</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Mir Mehrab Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mehrab Khan was the Khan of Kalat, ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baloch">Baloch</a> and Brahui tribal confederacy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Balochistan</a>, from 1817 to 1839. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-afghan-war">First Anglo-Afghan War</a> the British accused him of obstructing their army's march through the Bolan Pass, and on 13 November 1839 a British force stormed Kalat, where he was killed defending the citadel.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mehrab-khan.jpg" alt="Mehrab Khan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: WikiCobalt-Chloride · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FlagofKalat.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
